 a way forward</article-title><source>Clin Med</source><year>2007</year><volume>7</volume><fpage>232</fpage><lpage>234</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17633942</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lakhani</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A way forward</article-title><source>BMJ</source><year>2005</year><volume>330</volume><fpage>1326</fpage><lpage>1328</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15933359</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1136/bmj.330.7503.1326</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Preston</surname><given-names>LJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A survey of quality indicator use in the clinical laboratory</article-title><source>Clin Lab Sci</source><year>2008</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>25</fpage><lpage>32</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18335858</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rauch</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name><name><surname>Nichols</surname><given-names>JH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Laboratory accreditation and inspection</article-title><source>Clin Lab Med</source><year>2007</year><volume>27</volume><fpage>845</fpage><lpage>58</lpage><comment>vii</comment><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17950901</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.cll.2007.07.012</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lazda</surname><given-names>EJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Paediatric Histopathology EQA Participants' Annual Report and Minutes of Annual Meeting</article-title><source>Birmingham Women's Hospital</source><comment>April 27<sup>th </sup>2006</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Furness</surname><given-names>PN</given-names></name><name><surname>Lauder</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Response analysis in histopathology external quality assessment schemes</article-title><source>J Clin Pathol</source><year>1993</year><volume>46</volume><fpage>357</fpage><lpage>363</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8496394</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1136/jcp.46.4.357</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="other"><article-title>National Health Service Breast Screening Programme, Publication No. 57, External Quality Assessment Scheme for Breast Screening Histopathology, NHS Cancer Screening Programmes</article-title><year>1993</year></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Furness</surname><given-names>PN</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The United Kingdom National Renal Pathology External Quality Assessment Scheme</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.le.ac.uk/users/pnf1/eqa/"/></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>The Royal College of Pathologists</collab></person-group><article-title>Recommendations for the development of histopathology/cytopathology external quality assessment schemes</article-title><year>1998</year><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.rcpath.org/resources/pdf/G012-RecsForDevpmtOfHisto-CytoEQASchemes.pdf"/></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="other"><article-title>ILAC Guidelines for the Requirements for the Competence of Providers of Proficiency Testing Schemes ILAC-G13:08/2007</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.ilac.org/documents/ILAC_G13_08_2007.pdf"/></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dimech</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Report of Virtual Microscope Questionnaire Results (Commented by Prof D. Davies)</article-title><source>RCPA Quality Assurance Programs Pty Limited</source><comment>July 13<sup>th </sup>2005</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Barnes</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Pathology Modernisation Update</article-title><source>Pathology Modernisation 2002 LH1186 9th December 2002 Earl Court Conference Centre, London (UK) The Association of Clinical Biochemists Informa House, 30&#x02013;32 Mortimer Street, London</source></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Janus</surname><given-names>IL</given-names></name><name><surname>Groupthink</surname><given-names/></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Leavitt HJ, Pondy LR, Boje DM</surname></name></person-group><source>Readings in Managerial Psychology</source><year>1989</year><edition>4</edition><publisher-name>The University of Chicago Press, Chicago</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Shanteau</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Kein G, Salas E</surname></name></person-group><source>What does it mean when experts disagree?</source><year>2001</year><publisher-name>Naturalistic Decision Making, Lawrence Erlbaum Associates, Hillsdale NJ</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ruperto</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Meiorin</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Iusan</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name><name><surname>Ravelli</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Pistorio</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Martini</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Consensus procedures and their role in pediatric rheumatology</article-title><source>Curr Rheumatol Rep</source><year>2008</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>142</fpage><lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18460270</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s11926-008-0025-6</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hutchings</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Raine</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Sanderson</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Black</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A comparison of formal consensus methods used for developing clinical guidelines</article-title><source>J Health Serv Res Policy</source><year>2006</year><volume>11</volume><fpage>218</fpage><lpage>24</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17018195</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1258/135581906778476553</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Parham</surname><given-names>DM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Are external quality assurance (EQA) slide schemes a valid tool for the performance assessment of histopathologists?</article-title><source>Pathol Res Pract</source><year>2005</year><volume>201</volume><fpage>117</fpage><lpage>21</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15901132</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.prp.2005.01.004</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Meier-Ruge</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Hirschsprung's disease: its aetiology, pathogenesis and differential diagnosis</article-title><source>Curr Top Pathol</source><year>1974</year><volume>59</volume><fpage>131</fpage><lpage>79</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">4215624</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sch&#x000e4;rli</surname><given-names>AF</given-names></name><name><surname>Sossai</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Hypoganglionosis</article-title><source>Semin Pediatr Surg</source><year>1998</year><volume>7</volume><fpage>187</fpage><lpage>91</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9718658</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dahms</surname><given-names>BB</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Stocker JT, Dehner LP</surname></name></person-group><article-title>The gastrointestinal tract</article-title><source>Pediatric Pathology</source><volume>1</volume><edition>2</edition><publisher-name>Lippincott Williams &#x00026; Wilkins</publisher-name><fpage>631</fpage><lpage>703</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cree</surname><given-names>IA</given-names></name><name><surname>Guthrie</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Anderson</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><etal></etal></person-group><article-title>Departmental audit in histopathology</article-title><source>Pathol Res Pract</source><year>1993</year><volume>189</volume><fpage>453</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8351249</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B26"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Safrin</surname><given-names>RE</given-names></name><name><surname>Back</surname><given-names>CJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Surgical pathology signout &#x02013; routine review of every case by a 2nd pathologist</article-title><source>Am J Surg Pathol</source><year>1993</year><volume>17</volume><fpage>1190</fpage><lpage>2</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8214266</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00000478-199311000-00014</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B27"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lind</surname><given-names>AC</given-names></name><name><surname>Bewtra</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Healy</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><etal></etal></person-group><article-title>Prospective peer review in surgical pathology</article-title><source>Am J Surg Pathol</source><year>1995</year><volume>104</volume><fpage>560</fpage><lpage>6</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B28"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lesna</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Assessing diagnostic errors: when is suspension of a pathologist justified?</article-title><source>J Clin Pathol</source><year>1998</year><volume>51</volume><fpage>649</fpage><lpage>51</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9930066</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B29"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>De May</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>To err is human &#x02013; to sue [editorial]</article-title><source>Diagn Cytopathol</source><year>1996</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>iii</fpage><lpage>iv</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/(SICI)1097-0339(199609)15:3&#x0003c;I::AID-DC1&#x0003e;3.0.CO;2-4</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B30"><citation citation-type="other"><article-title>Data collected from the UKNEQAS in occasion of the Annual Meeting of the Pathological Society of Great Britain and Ireland in Glasgow 2007 (personal communication)</article-title></citation></ref><ref id="B31"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Favaloro</surname><given-names>EJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Standardization, Regulation, Quality Assurance and Emerging Technologies in Hemostasis: Issues, Controversies, Benefits, and Limitations</article-title><source>Semin Thromb Hemost</source><year>2007</year><volume>33</volume><fpage>290</fpage><lpage>298</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17427064</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1055/s-2007-971816</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>